**What this does:**

`<style>` is an HTML tag that lets you write CSS directly inside the HTML file.

- `:root { --green-dark: ... }` — defines two color variables. Instead of writing `#0d5c36` everywhere, you write `var(--green-dark)`. Change it in one place and it updates everywhere.
- `body { background: #f4f6f9 }` — sets the page background to a light grey
- `.dashboard-header` — styles the green header bar at the top. The `.` means "any HTML element that has `class="dashboard-header"`"
- `.upload-card` — styles the white card in the center. `border-radius: 12px` makes the corners rounded. `max-width: 560px` stops it from stretching too wide. `margin: 40px auto` centers it horizontally.

This is the same green color scheme as your dashboard — so both pages look like they belong to the same app.

